= Thought suppression — Simple =

'''Thought suppression''' is trying not to think about a particular thing.

The famous example is being told not to think about a white bear.

Older experiments found that the unwanted thought can sometimes come back more strongly later. This is called a rebound effect.

But the full research record is more complicated than the popular story.

People can sometimes suppress thoughts successfully, and rebound does not happen automatically in every study or situation.

Thought suppression is also different from trying to stop a memory from being retrieved.

